<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Khorezm People's Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1924 CE · capital Khiva</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived Soviet-backed republic that replaced the Khanate of Khiva in 1920 before being divided among the new national republics.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In early 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and the reformist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-khivans">Young Khivans</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-khiva">Khanate of Khiva</a>, then dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junaid-khan">Junaid Khan</a>. In April 1920 the Khorezm People's Soviet Republic was proclaimed, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Officially independent and allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>, it was governed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-khivans">Young Khivans</a> and later communists, under strong influence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. It nationalised the khan's estates, opened schools and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junaid-khan">Junaid Khan's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> forces. Purges in 1921 and 1922 removed many of the original leaders, and it became the Khorezm Soviet Socialist Republic in 1923.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the national delimitation of 1924 the republic was divided among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uzbek-ssr">Uzbek SSR</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turkmen-ssr">Turkmen SSR</a> and the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakalpak-autonomous-oblast">Karakalpak Autonomous Oblast</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karakalpakstan">Karakalpakstan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva's</a> walled inner town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itchan-kala">Itchan Kala</a>, survived and is now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khorezm-peoples-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Khorezm People's Soviet Republic" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Aivazovsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Khiva_1920-1923.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1924 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khiva</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Polvon Niyoz Yusupov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Uzbek, Turkmen, Karakalpak</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khorezm SSR, Khwarazm People's Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=khorezm-peoples-soviet-republic" aria-label="Khorezm People's Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6153 702 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khorezm People's Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6473 958L6473 958M6473 958L6691 960M6473 958L6455 1069"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6473 958h0M6691 960h0M6455 1069h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6473 958h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6473 958h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Khiva. <a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=khorezm-peoples-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
